WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.472
(gentle music)

00:00:02.472 --> 00:00:04.400
- Mazes are one of the
most fascinating things.

00:00:04.400 --> 00:00:06.072
Almost everybody, soon as they can crawl,

00:00:06.072 --> 00:00:08.311
are always wanting to
find out what's hidden,

00:00:08.311 --> 00:00:09.756
what's out of sight.

00:00:09.756 --> 00:00:12.601
(gentle music)

00:00:12.601 --> 00:00:15.997
My name's Adrian Fisher, I
live in Dorset, in England,

00:00:15.997 --> 00:00:19.551
and I create mazes and
labyrinths all over the world.

00:00:19.551 --> 00:00:22.551
(adventurous music)

00:00:27.041 --> 00:00:29.601
Well I spent the first few years

00:00:29.601 --> 00:00:32.158
of my career in accountancy.

00:00:32.158 --> 00:00:34.587
There came a moment when

00:00:34.587 --> 00:00:36.913
I'd created a maze in my father's garden,

00:00:36.913 --> 00:00:40.905
and then I started building
one, and two more and so on.

00:00:40.905 --> 00:00:42.128
And then I suddenly realized

00:00:42.128 --> 00:00:43.251
this was gonna be far more fulfilling

00:00:43.251 --> 00:00:45.571
if I spent my life creating mazes.

00:00:45.571 --> 00:00:48.023
This is the site of the place.

00:00:48.023 --> 00:00:51.989
This is 40 meters in diameter
and the maze is going here.

00:00:51.989 --> 00:00:55.239
Over the years I've created
mazes in some 40 countries,

00:00:55.239 --> 00:00:57.994
and I guess I've built over 700

00:00:57.994 --> 00:01:00.666
full-sized mazes in the landscape.

00:01:00.666 --> 00:01:04.943
I think that maze design
is a very esoteric art.

00:01:04.943 --> 00:01:07.759
You sketch out ideas and develop ideas

00:01:07.759 --> 00:01:09.799
on paper from drawings.

00:01:09.799 --> 00:01:12.097
But one of the exciting
things is a maze is a network.

00:01:12.097 --> 00:01:13.807
Now, a maze is a special kind of network

00:01:13.807 --> 00:01:16.086
where I decide there's
only one start point,

00:01:16.086 --> 00:01:18.191
I decide where the finish is,

00:01:18.191 --> 00:01:19.950
and I make sure that
every single bit of it

00:01:19.950 --> 00:01:23.782
can be as confusing or as easy as I wish.

00:01:23.782 --> 00:01:26.763
I'm trying to make it as
ingenious and tricky as possible, 

00:01:26.763 --> 00:01:28.662
but in the end I'm also an entertainer.

00:01:28.662 --> 00:01:30.734
I like to leave clues
that help you solve it

00:01:30.734 --> 00:01:32.397
and you feel so good about yourselves

00:01:32.397 --> 00:01:34.144
when you have beaten the maze designer.

00:01:34.144 --> 00:01:35.984
(adventurous music)

00:01:35.984 --> 00:01:38.563
Like a good movie you get to
the end and you're still...

00:01:38.563 --> 00:01:40.439
You don't want it to stop.

00:01:40.439 --> 00:01:43.505
(adventurous music)

00:01:43.505 --> 00:01:45.863
I'm appealing to some
basic instinct in us all

00:01:45.863 --> 00:01:49.248
that want to be entertained and explore

00:01:49.248 --> 00:01:53.067
and a maze is an ideal way of doing that.

00:01:53.067 --> 00:01:55.325
It's purpose is totally to one side

00:01:55.325 --> 00:01:58.407
of normal, sensible,
practical things in life,

00:01:58.407 --> 00:02:01.198
but gives so much pleasure
to so many millions.

00:02:01.198 --> 00:02:04.281
(adventurous music)

